>> title: Pollo Asado
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, mexican, achiote, citrus, grill, tacos
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: pollo, taco de pollo asado, tacos de pollo, grilled chicken, pollo a la parrilla, chicken asado
>> pairs-with: mexican-red-rice, corn-tortillas
>> servings: 6
>> time: 5 hr
>> step.1: blend the achiote adobo
>> step.2: marinate 4 hr
>> step.3: grill skin down 12 min, turn, 12 min
>> step.4: rest 10 min
>> step.5: chop off the bone, toss

Blend @achiote paste{2%Tbs}(recado rojo), @fresh orange juice{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @fresh lime juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @white vinegar{2%Tbs}, @garlic{5%cloves}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @ground allspice{1/4%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1%Tbs} smooth in a #blender{}.

Marinate @bone-in chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; skin on) in @&(~1)adobo{} for ~marinate{4%hr} in the fridge, working it under the skin.

Grill @&(~1)marinated chicken{} skin down over medium coals in a #charcoal grill{} for ~grill{12%min}, until the skin lifts free of the bars on its own, then turn it and grill ~grill{12%min} more, to 175°F (79°C) at the bone.

Rest @&(~1)grilled chicken{} for ~rest{10%min}.

Chop @&(~1)rested chicken{} off the bone, skin and all, and toss it with @white onion{1/2%cup}(chopped), @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped), and @fresh lime juice{1%Tbs}.
